/target
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock.bak

# Stray rustc artifacts from differential-hunt / e2e probes that compile a
# transpiled lib in-place (a `rustc lib.rs` with no `-o` emits `lib*.rlib` in the
# CWD). These must never be committed (PMAT-689 leaked one via `git add -A`).
*.rlib
*.rmeta
*.o

# Python bytecode (e2e fixtures are run through python3 for cross-checking)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store

# Caches
.cache/
~/.cache/xpile/
.pmat/
.pv/

# Lean / Lake build artifacts (PMAT-903 proof-lane `lake build`). The
# `lakefile.lean`, `lean-toolchain`, and `lake-manifest.json` ARE committed
# (they pin the build); the compiled `.lake/` output tree is not.
.lake/

# Local config
.env
.env.local

# Claude Code session-local artifacts (transcripts, paste-cache,
# scheduled-tasks state, etc.) — but DO check in the slash-command
# skills under .claude/commands/ so the repo ships its dogfood
# workflow. The `.claude/*` (trailing `*`) form makes git evaluate
# each direct child individually so the `!.claude/commands/`
# exception takes effect.
.claude/*
!.claude/commands/
